{"name":"Cordwood","hex":"#594035","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"cordwood","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Wood suitable for use as firewood; firewood cut and split into conveniently sized pieces for easy stacking into cords.","Split and cut wood as an economic commodity."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cordwood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Cordwood construction","blocks":[{"text":"Cordwood construction is a term used for a natural building method in which short logs are piled crosswise to build a wall, using mortar or cob to permanently secure them. This technique can be made to use a wide variety of locally available materials at minimal financial cost, and is a classic example of trading a higher raw labor requirement for technical ease and cost-efficiency of building."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/34/Cordwood_masonry_wall.jpg/330px-Cordwood_masonry_wall.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cordwood_construction"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Cordwoodhouse.jpg/330px-Cordwoodhouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/43/Cordwoodhouse.jpg/330px-Cordwoodhouse.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A section of a cordwood home","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACordwoodhouse.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/That_Roundhouse_cordwood.jpg/500px-That_Roundhouse_cordwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9a/That_Roundhouse_cordwood.jpg/500px-That_Roundhouse_cordwood.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"That Roundhouse was 